url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-factory-runners%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-factory-runners%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/software-factory-runners%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary for non-engineers\n\n- Avoid phone work for documentation-only changes.\n- Keep every required phone check covered.\n- Keep full nightly and manual phone checks.\n\nTicket: https://app.hypertask.ai/detail/project-11514/169\n\n## Change\n\nAndroid tests now route phone work using the real PR merge-base diff. Six existing phone contexts always start and validate the routing result; only heavy steps are conditional. Unknown paths and empty diffs require phones. Router failure fails phone contexts. Add `phone-routing` to the local complete-check gate alongside every existing required context; no required check removed or weakened.\n\nFive optional phone workflows additionally cover Gradle root inputs, wrappers and the shared action. Existing nightly/manual coverage and cancellation remain intact.\n\nThe first remote run exposed two blockers: the local complete-check list omitted the new router; the native-skills driver consumed stale UI XML after UiAutomator reported a null root. The follow-up adds the router requirement and clears old device/local XML, bounds null-root retries to three, captures both output streams, and propagates selection failures. It preserves journey assertions and adds host regression cases for stdout/stderr null roots, exhausted retries, missing dumps, transport/timeout failures, plus a stderr-capture negative control.\n\n## Verification\n\nNo builds or tests run on the VPS. Routing regression tests run in GitHub before phone dispatch, exercising real temporary Git histories: docs-only, mixed, deletion, rename, advanced base, missing/invalid revisions. Source guards cover required phone contexts, optional inputs, nightly/manual coverage and cancellation.\n\nInitial head `e2732a00cda1de908b27e0b2883ccbfa788fc98d`: router and all six phone jobs succeeded; `test` and `verify` failed with the diagnosed errors above. Follow-up head `c5ed49e9df1dd12ef6b35e0965057827cdd55fee`: all contexts except `test` succeeded; Python AST parsing exposed missing method-call parentheses in the new regression test. One-line syntax repair pushed as `d41e99db363415b0b4d6464227321f6e77a15ab6`. At 2026-11-07T10:13Z the new router, secret scan and paid-AI guard passed; app and phone checks were running. No complete-green, merge or shipment claim. `git diff --check` clean.\n\n## Real timing evidence — inconclusive\n\nPhone-job wall span **735s before → 386s after** (one actual run each; queue excluded). Six successful phone jobs aggregate 2465s before versus 1482s after. These are different relevant app/workflow commits, not docs-only controls; cache/host variability is uncontrolled. Both actually ran all six phone proofs. **Not evidence of routing speedup.**\n\nBefore: https://github.com/valentinyeo/multiprompt-android/actions/runs/42288577129\n\nAfter (initial PR head): https://github.com/valentinyeo/multiprompt-android/actions/runs/42357692432\n\nStill required: comparable real unrelated-change routing timing, current-head green checks, default-branch shipment, and a full day of eligible quiet Android slowdown alarms. Do not close from a single faster sample.\n\n## Risk and rollback\n\nExclusions remain narrow: docs, root Markdown, and release-note paths only. No app behavior, signing, billing, paid service or repository branch-protection settings changed. Revert this PR to restore unconditional phone work.\n\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-07T08:58:09Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T10:13:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"b417b4cf896421f92843833e4b9bc239cd6496d9","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"